--- body ---
## Context
The committed `bench/query_arms.mjs` reads each arm's `MIN_MATCH_TERMS` /
`isStopword` exports for its fallback bookkeeping. The 0091 series (fork
branches `pr2-expansion`, `pr3-droplist-r5`, upstream PRs #46/#47) no longer
exports either — pruning lives in `pruneTerms`. Run against r5-shaped arms,
the committed driver would silently mis-report the fallback columns while the
latency columns look fine (found during the r5 full-stack re-measurement,
ticket 0091 log 2026-09-01; the measurement used an adapted runner reading
each arm's own `pruneTerms`, left at `~/data/projets/zoteus-bench/query_arms_r5.mjs`).

## Actions
1. Port the adapted per-arm `pruneTerms` introspection into
   `bench/query_arms.mjs` (or absorb `query_arms_r5.mjs` as its successor),
   keeping compatibility with pre-r5 arms or failing loudly on them.
2. Fold in the shared `rbo`/`pct` helpers duplicated with
   `bench/query_arms_multi.mjs` (deferred by the 2026-09-01 gaze simplify
   pass as out-of-diff).

## Test
A fixture arm without `MIN_MATCH_TERMS`/`isStopword` exports: the driver must
either report correct fallback columns via `pruneTerms` or refuse — never
report zeros silently.

## Exit criteria
- [x] driver measures r5-shaped arms with correct fallback columns
- [x] loud failure (not silent zeros) on an arm shape it cannot introspect
- [x] `make check` green
